[38.806908, "o", "I wrote `brain/tools/release-kit.md` as a repo tool. I only read the README and the two scripts and ran nothing.\r\n\r\nThe `description` line is:\r\n\r\n> Shell scripts to cut a git release: print a changelog from commits since the last tag, and tag and push v<version>. Use when preparing or publishing a release of any repo.\r\n\r\nIs that right?\r\n\r\nThe entry also says to confirm the version and commit with you before running `tag.sh`, since it pushes a tag to the remote. I added that on my own, so tell me if you'd rather drop it.\r\n"]
