[101.559556, "o", "The project is set up and builds with `cargo build`.\r\n\r\n- **Name:** `amber-heron`. This session was non-interactive, so I took the first candidate from the naming rule (colour + animal). The other four were coral-badger, slate-finch, olive-newt and indigo-lynx.\r\n- **Path:** `~/demo/code/amber-heron`\r\n- **Why a subfolder:** the current folder wasn't empty (it holds `release-kit`), so I created a new folder inside it.\r\n- **Created:**\r\n  - the `cargo init` output: `Cargo.toml`, `src/main.rs`, `.gitignore` and a git repo\r\n  - `CLAUDE.md`, with the purpose and the build, test and run commands\r\n  - a line in `projects.md` in your brain folder, which didn't exist yet, so I created it\r\n- **Not done:** nothing is committed, and there are no features or example code beyond the `cargo init` scaffold.\r\n- **Preferences applied:**\r\n  - Rust edition 2021.\r\n  - No dependencies added, since your Rust preferences say to ask first.\r\n  - The imperative-mood rule fo"]
[101.559585, "o", "r commit messages is noted for when you commit.\r\n- **Tools used:** `naming`. `release-kit` and `reviewer` weren't relevant to starting a project.\r\n- **Defaults I picked:** none. Your preferences covered every choice.\r\n\r\nTo start working there:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd ~/demo/code/amber-heron && claude\r\n```\r\n"]
