[117.030655, "o", "**Preferences that apply**\r\n\r\nThis is a Rust project, so both saved preference files apply:\r\n- **General:** Write git commit messages in the imperative mood, such as \"Add parser\".\r\n- **Rust:**\r\n  - Use edition 2021.\r\n  - Ask before adding any dependency to `Cargo.toml`.\r\n\r\n**Tools I can call on**\r\n- **naming** (notes): Rules for naming a new project, a colour and an animal joined by a hyphen. `amber-heron` already follows this, so I don't need it now.\r\n- **release-kit** (repo): Shell scripts that print a changelog from commits since the last tag, and tag and push `v<version>`. I'd use it when preparing or publishing a release.\r\n- **reviewer** (expert session): A code-review expert. I'd send it a diff and what the change is for, and it replies with findings. It's useful for a second review before a commit or PR. If that session isn't running, I'd tell you rather than guess its answer.\r\n\r\nI haven't opened the per-tool files in `brain/tools/`. I'd read each one before using that tool.\r\n"]
[117.050187, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[119.074862, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# That's dotfactory.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
